You can ftp from lampwick.berkeley.edu or psuvm.psu.edu.

I have been making it available to those inside IBM by mail at cost
(about $3.00US for 5.25" 1.2 Meg. disk or $3.70 3.5" disk). I use the
excess disk real estate to include NNANSI.SYS, VANSI.SYS, and FRACTINT
ver. 10 from the Simtel collections, as well. Sorry no 360K disks, as
the archive file is 388K for NetHack alone. I'll take requests from
people outside of IBM, as well. Just mail to the address in my
signature. Oh yeah, Canadian postage is running an addition $0.09 and
I'll know UK postage costs this Saturday. 

I have also uploaded it to numerous Austin bulletin boards, and I
included the number for one that supports 9600HST transfers in my last
posting to the group, under UK distribution or something like that.

